meta {
  name: Load Underlying
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/options/load/AAPL
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Load Options — One Underlying

  Generates + loads option contracts for a SINGLE underlying and stores the result.
  Same logic as "Load All" but scoped to one symbol — handy for iterating on a
  symbol's strike increment or DTE without reloading everything.

  ## Path
  - `/{underlying}` — the underlying stock symbol (e.g. AAPL). It should be present
    in `option-tickers.txt` so its per-symbol increment is picked up; if not, the
    default increment is used.

  ## Response (200) — full per-contract detail
  {
    underlying, spot, expiry, strikeIncrement, contracts, loaded, error?, loadedAt,
    contractDetail: [ { occSymbol, type, strike, moneyness (ITM|OTM), expiry,
                        barCount, loaded, error? } ]
  }

  ## Notes
  - Never throws — a missing spot or an unlisted strike is captured in `error`
    (top-level for the underlying, or per-contract in `contractDetail`).
}
